<title>USA: Tenn. $82 mln notes yield 3.60 pct - Smith Barney.</title>
<headline>Tenn. $82 mln notes yield 3.60 pct - Smith Barney.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Wednesday it priced $81.6 million Tennessee general obligation weekly variable rate notes, series E, at an initial rate of 3.60 percent with a 3.60 percent coupon.</p>
<p>The notes are dated Nov 27, 1996 and due July 2, 2001. They are rated MIG-1/VMIG-1 by Moody's Investors Service Inc and SP1-plus/A1-plus by Standard &amp; Poor's Corp.</p>
<p>The firm also priced a $3 million taxable series F weekly floater note with a 5.40 percent coupon to yield 5.40 percent. The notes are due July 2, 2001.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
